Subject: [PATCH] ao_mediafoundation: play E-AC-3 through the system decoder

FFmpeg decodes only the 5.1/7.1 bed of a Dolby Atmos (JOC) E-AC-3 track, and
ao_wasapi can pass the bitstream on only in exclusive mode, to a device that
decodes it. Headphones and built-in speakers with a Windows spatial sound
format (Dolby Atmos for Headphones, ...) therefore never get the objects.

This AO takes the E-AC-3 access units back out of the IEC 61937 stream
ad_spdif produces and serves them to a Media Foundation session from a media
source of its own. The topology loader inserts the Dolby decoder MFT, which
negotiates MFAudioFormat_Float_SpatialObjects with the audio renderer. The
session's presentation clock is the audio clock.

It sits after wasapi in the autoprobe order: a receiver that takes the
bitstream keeps getting it. It refuses to initialize when the decoder would
not output objects (no spatial format on the endpoint, no decoder), so every
other setup keeps today's path.

mf.dll and mfplat.dll are loaded when the AO is first asked for rather than
imported, so the player still starts on Windows editions that ship without
the media features.

Tested on a bench that drives the driver like audio/out/buffer.c does (start,
pause, reset, underrun, end, reload, device selection). The revision before
this one, which imported the two DLLs, was also tested in a libmpv build with
a video window and inside Plezy (pause, seeks, volume, end of file).
