  audio/out/ao.c                 |    5 +
  audio/out/ao_mediafoundation.c | 1259 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
  meson.build                    |    8 +
  4 files changed, 1294 insertions(+)

diff --git a/DOCS/man/ao.rst b/DOCS/man/ao.rst
index 7eb7c97..cae6032 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/ao.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/ao.rst
@@ -321,3 +321,25 @@ Available audio output drivers are:
         cases, but reportedly on some devices there are glitches following
         stream resets under the default setting. In such cases, specifying a
         shorter duration might help.
+
+``mediafoundation``
+    Dolby Digital Plus through the decoder Windows ships (Media Foundation).
+
+    Used for E-AC-3 that mpv passes through (``--audio-spdif=eac3``). Instead
+    of sending the bitstream to the device, it hands the access units to the
+    system's Dolby decoder. With a spatial sound format active on the device
+    (Dolby Atmos for Headphones, for home theater, for built-in speakers) the
+    decoder renders a Dolby Atmos track as objects, which mpv's own decoder
+    cannot do. It comes after ``wasapi`` in the autoprobe order, so a device
+    that takes the bitstream itself still gets it.
+
+    The output refuses to initialize, and mpv falls back to the next one or to
+    its own decoder, when no decoder on the system offers spatial objects for
+    the device. It plays on the default device, or on the device selected with
+    ``--audio-device=wasapi/{id}``.
+
+    The following global options are supported by this audio output:
+
+    ``--ao-mediafoundation-require-spatial=<yes|no>``
+        Whether to refuse when the decoder would output plain PCM (default:
+        yes).
